 "notes": "Chart Thirteen ledger (right page of spread c-71) covers 1939-08-26 (SAT.AUG26) through 1939-10-07 (SAT.7); all dated rows fall in calendar year 1939 (the \"1939\" label sits mid-header, above the DATE row, marking the last of three carried-forward pivotal-point groups, not a mid-chart year change). Row/date mapping verified via 1939 calendar (Sept 4 Labor Day and all Sundays correctly absent from the ledger) and cross-checked using the six printed annotations on the left page (126), each of which names a date and a ledger column that matches the handwritten entry found there. Every US+BS=KP checksum across all dated rows and the row-2/row-4 header groups balances exactly. The sole exception is the topmost header group: US DT \"43 1/4\" + BS DT \"50 1/4\" = 93 1/2, but KP DT is written \"93 7/8\" (a 3/8-point discrepancy); all three digits were independently re-verified at high zoom and are transcribed as actually written rather than force-fit to the checksum. Column identity for entries in the four \"blue\" columns (SR/NR/NRC/SRC) was cross-validated two ways: (1) direct alignment against the printed vertical column-header labels in high-resolution crops, and (2) matching to the six dated annotations, which explicitly state the column name for six of the rows (Aug29=Natural Rally, Sept2=Upward Trend, Sept14=Natural Reaction, Sept19=Natural Rally, Sept28=Secondary Reaction, Oct6=Secondary Rally) \u2014 both methods agree. Underline colors reported reflect only heavier hand-drawn strokes confined to a single number's width; the thin light-blue horizontal rules and the periodic full-page-width red rules (row-group/Saturday dividers) present throughout the ledger are printed grid features, not hand underlines, and were excluded even where they happen to coincide with a written price.",
